course: dictionary
lesson: 1493
title: Caveman: a person from long ago, and a rude nickname
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A caveman is a person from the Stone Age, a very long time ago. People imagine cavemen living in caves, but many early humans lived in huts and tents too, so the picture of cavemen only in caves is not the whole story.
explain: «In cartoons cavemen ride dinosaurs.» That is a joke, not history. Dinosaurs died out about 66 million years before the first humans, so they never met. When you read a story, ask yourself: could this really have happened?
explain: The word has a second meaning too. Informally, a caveman is a rough or old-fashioned man with rude manners. If a friend calls you a caveman, they are teasing you. Check the tone of the sentence to see if it is a joke or an insult.
fact: A caveman is a person from very long ago, in the Stone Age.
fact: Cavemen are imagined as living in caves, but many early humans lived in huts and tents too.
fact: Informally, a caveman is a rough or old-fashioned man with rude manners.
fact: «Cartoon cavemen who grunt and ride dinosaurs are pure fantasy.»
fact: Dinosaurs died out about 66 million years before the first humans.
exercise: «In cartoons cavemen ride dinosaurs.» Is this true? | Only in films, which are always true | Yes, dinosaurs and cavemen lived side by side | Yes, every caveman had a pet dinosaur | *No, dinosaurs died out long before the first humans
exercise: Which word means a person from very long ago, in the Stone Age? | Fossil | Dinosaur | Cartoon | *Caveman
exercise: Early humans sheltered in caves, but many also lived where? | In space | *In huts and tents | In the sea | Inside a dinosaur
test: The Flintstones shows cavemen keeping dinosaurs as pets. Why is this not real? | Dinosaurs only lived in the sea | Dinosaurs were too fast to keep | Cavemen were too small to keep dinosaurs | *Dinosaurs were gone 66 million years before the first humans
test: Your friend says, «You are such a caveman!» at the dinner table. What does caveman mean here? | A cave with paintings on the wall | A type of dinosaur | A friendly teacher who explains things | *A rough, rude man who acts old-fashioned
exam: Which sentence is a real fact, not a cartoon? | Caveman means only a rude man | Cavemen kept dinosaurs as pets | Cartoon cavemen ride dinosaurs | *Dinosaurs died out about 66 million years before the first humans
